-- Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 - its 23 power armors, robots and
-- vehicles, with 158 M.D.C. locations and 122 weapon-system entries.
--
--   Empire of the Sun, printed 59-67: Nazca Power Armor, Armor of the Sun,
--     Atahualpa Combat Suit, Solar Combat Armor, Slinger Light Tank
--   The Arkhons, printed 84-97: Stormwind exoskeleton, Ghost Wasp, Death
--     Cyclops, Great Cyclops robot, "Porcupine" T-10 tank, "Evil Eye" APC,
--     Spikefish fighter
--   The Megaversal Legion, printed 116-121: Counterstrike power armor,
--     Neo-Abrams, Neo-Bradley, Neo-Apache
--   The Silver River Republics, printed 168-183: Mecha-Lizard, Toro
--     "Minotaur", Glitter Boy Number 7, Mastodon and Galapagos robots, Puma
--     tank, Hussar APC
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-south-america-2-vehicles.sql
--
-- ALL 23 ARE NEW. catalog-diff --table vehicles --remote, 2026-09-25, run
-- immediately before this file, matched none of them, and none of the slugs
-- exists in production.
--
-- READ FROM A SCAN (no text layer). Extracted in three slices by
-- book-extract-worker, every M.D.C. table and weapon block checked against a
-- render; book-reconcile then checked all 23 against the pages. Printed 85 is
-- a full-page illustration, empty in the cache and losing nothing.
--
-- READ OFF A RENDER WHERE THE OCR WAS WRONG:
--   printed 170  the Mecha-Lizard's model is PA-10ML (the OCR reads PA-1OML)
--   printed 180  the Puma's location is the Rail Gun Cupola (OCR: Cygola)
--   printed 119-121  the "Sensors, etc." entries close the Neo-Abrams (8),
--                Neo-Bradley (5) and Neo-Apache (7) Weapon Systems lists; the
--                OCR drops each number. They are not weapons, but the book
--                numbers them there, so they are rows here, as the force
--                fields are.
--
-- BOOK SLIPS, stored as printed and noted on the row: the Neo-Abrams heading
-- says M10A1 and its stat block MBT-10A1; the Toro's Energy Axe M.D.C. carries
-- a degree mark where the others carry asterisks; the Atahualpa's chest guns
-- mix S.D.C. and M.D. in one entry.
--
-- ARMOR OF THE SUN HAS NO mdc_main_body: its M.D.C. is set by the wearer's
-- M.E., so every location carries the formula in mdc_note and mdc NULL.
--
-- PRICES: a black-market range stores its low end; an open-ended figure
-- ("upwards of", "50+ million") is cost NULL with the figure in cost_note.
--
-- DESCRIPTIONS ARE PARAPHRASES, never the book's prose.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles
  (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, cost, cost_note, description, source_book)
VALUES
  ('nazca-power-armor', 'Nazca Power Armor (NPA Mark I)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 1, NULL, 'Running 60 mph (96 kmph) maximum, does not tire the pilot; Leaping up to 30 feet (9.1 m) high or across', 'Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 11 feet (3.3 m); Width: 6 feet (1.8 m); Length: 4 feet, 6 inches (1.4 m)', '1.3 tons fully loaded', 600, NULL, 'Not for sale; only issued to Empire of the Sun loyalists. Stolen/captured suits sold on the black market would cost upwards of 10 million credits, and their magical energy life will only last 1D4 years.', 'Model Type NPA Mark I, a Heavy Armored Infantry Assault Suit, a joint Inca-Nazca creation powered entirely by magic (one of the few techno-wizard items in the Empire), in service for the last 5 years. Physical Strength equal to a supernatural P.S. of 35. The suit is soft M.D.C. armor at baseline, energized by Nazca line patterns inscribed on it: when magically activated (up to 8 hours per 24-hour day), a skin-tight energy field raises its M.D.C. dramatically and grants supernatural strength and speed to the wearer, and the forearm blades become lethal mega-damage weapons; the suit also regenerates to full M.D.C. at the start of each new day. No cargo capacity. Magical energies need replenishing every five years; only about 100 suits are produced per year, with roughly 250 in service, 65 destroyed, and 30 missing or captured.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.59-61'),
  ('armor-of-the-sun', 'Armor of the Sun (SOL-I)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 1, NULL, 'Running 100 mph (160 kmph) maximum, does not tire the operator', 'Flying 200 mph (320 kmph) maximum; maximum altitude 15,000 feet (4572 m); range limited to 12 hours of activation per day, for a maximum of 2400 miles (3840 km) per day', NULL, 'Height: 7 feet (2.1 m); Width: 4 feet (1.2 m); Length: 3 feet (0.9 m)', '800 lbs. (362.4 kg)', NULL, NULL, 'Never sold by the Empire of the Sun; a stolen amulet could cost as much as 10+ million credits.', 'Model Type SOL-I, a Magical Construct Assault System: not a true suit of power armor but a holy talisman of the Pantheon of the Sun (a golden medallion) that, when activated by touch and concentration, replaces the wearer with a huge burning golden humanoid figure. About 100 amulets exist, held only by loyal Inca Warriors, demigods and champions. Physical Strength is a supernatural P.S. of 40. It has no technological sensors, radio or communication gear, but has magical equivalents: an environmental system, the ability to see the invisible and sense magic (2000 ft/610 m), and telepathic communication with a psychic or magician up to one mile away. It carries no cargo; clothes, body armor and carried weapons vanish when activated and reappear afterward. It can be activated up to six times a day for up to two hours each; if destroyed it cannot reactivate for 24 hours but fully regenerates by then, and damage otherwise carries over between activations, healing at 1D6x10 M.D. per hour. The armor takes no damage from flame attacks and half damage from energy attacks. Power system is magical, recharged with 1,000 P.P.E. every two years.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.61-63'),
  ('atahualpa-combat-suit', 'Atahualpa Combat Suit (AC-1)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 1, NULL, 'Running 50 mph (80 kmph) maximum; tires the operator but at only 30 percent of the usual fatigue rate', 'Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 8 feet (2.4 m); Width: 6 feet (1.8 m); Length: 4 feet (1.2 m)', '1,200 lb. (544 kg)', 200, 1500000, '1.5 million credits', 'Model Type AC-1, an Infantry Combat Exoskeleton: the first working power armor model developed by Arequipa armorers, in service for over two centuries and still the Empire most commonly produced suit, with over 5,000 still in military service plus thousands more with militias. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 30. Fully sealed with no apparent eyes (sensors hidden two-way-mirror style); a featureless, square helmet, solid torso block joined by a flexible midsection to a smaller pelvis block, thin arms and legs with cartoonish elbows, knees, hands and feet. Three mini-missiles are mounted over each shoulder. As a primary sidearm it carries an oversized Illapa rifle with a larger drum magazine; two chest guns fire conventional S.D.C. bullets or explosive M.D. rounds as a back-up. No cargo capacity. Power system is nuclear, average energy life 10 years.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.63-64'),
  ('solar-combat-armor', 'Solar Combat Armor (SC-Mark III)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 1, NULL, 'Running 60 mph (96 kmph)', 'Flying 400 mph (640 kmph) maximum; can fly for up to 24 hours without overheating; maximum altitude 20,000 feet (6096 m)', NULL, 'Height: 7 feet (2.1 m); Width: 4 feet (1.2 m); Length: 3 feet (0.9 m)', '500 lbs. (226.5 kg)', 320, 20000000, '20 million credits', 'Model Type SC-Mark III, an Airborne Assault Exoskeleton with Plasma Field System: a technological answer to the Armor of the Sun, developed with New Babylon D-Bee Guild engineers after Arequipan armorers could not master the flame-covered concept alone. Assembled in Arequipa by 100 P.A., though many parts still must be imported from New Babylon. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 35. Magnetic field generators and plasma dischargers coat the suit in a constant plasma flux about an inch off the surface, projecting 90 percent of the heat outward and igniting or melting anything it touches; the field can be shut off instantly to confuse heat-seeking sensors, but while on it makes the suit detectable for miles and vulnerable to heat sensors. No cargo capacity. Power system is nuclear, average energy life 15 years; high cost limits how many the Empire can field.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.64-66'),
  ('slinger-light-tank', 'Slinger Light Tank (H1-C or H1-L)', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 2, NULL, '60 mph (96 kmph) maximum; cruising speed typically 40 mph (64 kmph); range 400 miles (640 km) with electric or combustion engine', 'Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 7 feet (2.1 m); Width: 6 feet (1.8 m); Length: 9 feet (2.7 m)', '5 tons', 220, 90000, '90,000 credits with all weapon systems', 'Model Type H1-C or H1-L, a Light Battle Tank and the only armored vehicle built in the Empire of the Sun, manufactured in Arequipa and crewed by a driver and a gunner-commander whose seat rotates with the turret. The tank is tiny, barely taller than a human. The turret mounts either a conventional 90mm cannon (H1-C, about 60 percent of tanks) or a laser cannon (H1-L, about 40 percent), plus a coaxial 15mm machinegun and an automatic grenade launcher; the pilot has a bow-mounted machinegun of the same make. Not nuclear powered (hard to manufacture in the Empire); runs on diesel or electric engines instead. Cargo is a small storage compartment for two energy rifles and two 1-foot-square (0.3x0.3 m) areas for personal effects. Despite being lightly powered and armored, entire armored divisions rely on it against the more advanced Arkhon war machines.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.66-67'),
  ('stormwind-assault-exoskeleton', 'Stormwind Assault Exoskeleton (LE-457S)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 1, 0, '50 mph (80 kmph) maximum running; running tires the operator at only 30% of the usual fatigue rate', '200 mph (320 kmph) maximum flying; cruising speed typically 80-100 mph (120-160 kmph); no limit to altitude, can reach outer space', NULL, 'Height: adds 4 inches (10 cm) to wearer''s height (personally fitted). Width: 4 inches (10 cm) wider than normal. Length: 2 inches (5 cm) longer than normal.', '150 lbs. (67.5 kg) for the suit', 150, 1000000, 'Not for sale; captured suits typically sell for 1-2 million credits depending on condition. Weapons manufacturers (CS, Northern Gun, Triax, Splugorth, Naruni) would pay up to 5 million for a new, undamaged, complete suit if they knew of the antigravity system.', 'A light armored-infantry exoskeleton, standard issue to about one-third of Arkhon line soldiers, with flying capability via an integral antigravity system but without power armor combat bonuses. P.S. equal to 22. Powered by a long-life battery averaging 2 years of energy life (Arkhon-exclusive tech, estimated 2D4x10 years for Rifts Earth to duplicate). Carries no cargo. Its primary weapon is a pick among the Arkhon rifles: Stormwind troopers are typically assigned a TB-Prime Rifle (60%), FR-5 Flechette Rifle (15%), M-100 Energy Machinegun (10%), BM-2 Mortar (5%), BRL-3 Rocket Launcher (5%), or FRA-1 Auto-cannon (5%), plus a built-in TB-9 tri-beam wrist pistol as backup. In hand to hand combat it has no special bonuses but inflicts 2D6+7 S.D.C. from punches and 4D6+7 S.D.C. from kicks, and lets the wearer carry heavy loads at 30% of the usual fatigue rate.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.84-86'),
  ('ghost-wasp-aerial-power-armor', 'Ghost Wasp Aerial Power Armor (APA-III)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 1, 0, '50 mph (80 kmph)', '600 mph (960 kmph) maximum; cruising speed 100-300 mph (160-480 kmph); Stealth System disengages automatically above 100 mph (162.5 kmph); no altitude limit, can reach outer space', NULL, 'Height: 7 feet (2.1 m) standing. Width: 4 feet 7 inches (1.4 m). Length: 14 feet (4.25 m) head to stinger tip.', '1 ton fully loaded', 350, 7000000, 'Not for sale; only available at the Arkhon Freehold. Captured/patched second-hand suits found in South America typically have 20% less M.D.C. and are missing one or two major weapon systems, and cost 7-10 million credits.', 'A stealth-capable dragonfly-like heavy power armor with an advanced holographic chameleon system that masks it from visual, radar, infrared and thermal detection (only a 21% chance of a thermal reading, and even then it looks unusual). Stealth only functions below 100 mph and while not firing weapons; using a weapon or exceeding that speed shuts the system off. P.S. equal to 35, powered by a nuclear system with about 20 years of energy life; must cool off after 6 hours of flight above 300 mph or 15 hours at cruising speed or below. Carries no cargo. Can be reconfigured as a long-range bomber (trading the flechette rifle for up to four long-range missiles, with reduced speed/maneuverability until they are launched). Power armor bonuses: +1 attack per melee at levels 1, 6 and 12 (besides the pilot''s own); +1 to dodge at levels 3, 7 and 11; +1 to roll with punch, fall or impact; critical strike as the pilot''s.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.86-89'),
  ('death-cyclops-assault-suit', 'Death Cyclops Assault Suit (APA-9)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 1, 0, '80 mph (128 kmph) maximum; running tires the operator at only 10% the normal rate', 'Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 9 feet (2.7 m). Width: 6 feet (1.8 m). Length: 4 feet (1.2 m).', '1 ton', 450, 5000000, 'Not for sale. Captured/stolen suits are extremely rare on the South American Black Market: 11 million for a new, undamaged suit (almost unheard of) to 5 million for a partially rebuilt suit (permanently reduced M.D.C. by 25%, tri-beam system replaced by lasers doing 1D6 to 4D6 M.D., shoulder weapon replaced with a rail gun or similar large energy weapon).', 'The standard assault suit of the Arkhon Armored Cavalry, shaped like a humanoid predator from the Arkhon homeworld, with broad armored shoulders, oversized arms, and slender legs; the pilot''s tail tucks inside the torso. P.S. equal to 45, powered by an anti-matter system with about 25 years of energy life. Carries no cargo. Four hidden torso tri-beams supplement a shoulder-mounted flechette gun or tri-beam rifle, and the suit can mount optional back modules (mini-missiles, two anti-aircraft variants, or a mortar). Vibro-field forearm spikes add mega-damage in hand to hand. Power armor bonuses: +1 attack per melee at levels 1, 6 and 12 (besides the pilot''s own); +1 to dodge at levels 1, 4, 8 and 12; +2 to roll with punch, fall or impact; +1 to pull punch; critical strike as the pilot''s.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.88-91'),
  ('great-cyclops-assault-robot', 'Great Cyclops Assault Robot (AB-17)', 'rifts', 'robot', 1, 3, '100 mph (160 kmph) maximum; running does not tire the pilot', '400 mph (640 kmph) maximum; cruising speed typically 100-200 mph (160-320 kmph); no altitude limit, can reach outer space', NULL, 'Height: 35 feet (10.5 m). Width: 16 feet (4.8 m). Length: 8 feet (2.4 m).', '35 tons', 750, 50000000, 'Not for sale; no stolen or rebuilt unit has ever reached the market (pilots fight to the death or self-destruct rather than surrender). If ever available, would cost 50+ million credits.', 'A gigantic robot version of the Death Cyclops, roughly three times its size, standing on two stilt-like legs that plant into the ground for stability, and capable of flight. All weapons are built into the body rather than carried, so they can only be silenced by destroying the robot itself. P.S. equal to 55, powered by an anti-matter system with about 25 years of energy life; must cool off after 6 hours of flight above 200 mph or 12 hours at cruising speed. Cargo is a small locker for a pistol/sub-machinegun and personal effects. The pilot''s compartment seats three additional passengers. Vibro-spikes on the forearms boost hand to hand damage to near-supernatural levels. Robot bonuses: +1 attack per melee at levels 1, 5 and 10 (besides the pilot''s own); +1 to dodge at levels 1 and 8; +2 to roll with punch, fall or impact; critical strike as the pilot''s.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.91-93'),
  ('porcupine-t-10-assault-tank', '"Porcupine" T-10 Assault Tank', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 6, 0, '200 mph (320 kmph) maximum, hovercraft system', 'Not possible; hover cannot lift the tank more than 5 feet (1.5 m) off any surface without losing pressure and sinking back down', 'Can cross water for short distances only', 'Height: 12 feet (3.65 m). Width: 13 feet (3.9 m). Length: 20 feet (6.1 m).', '70 tons fully loaded', 600, 10000000, 'Not for sale. 3% chance per month a captured tank can be found on the black market; such a tank would have 1D4x10% less M.D.C., be missing 1D4 weapon systems, and cost 10-20 million credits.', 'The Arkhons'' main battle tank, styled with a stylized ''Eye'' beneath the main turret and covered in spine-like protrusions, hence its nickname. Its main turret mounts two over-and-under cannons (each a tri-beam weapon over a conventional cannon), with two side tri-beam mini-turrets, a rear box mini-missile turret, a flechette gun cupola atop the turret for anti-missile defense, and two bow-mounted flechette mini-turrets. Crewed by six: four gunners, a driver and a commander. Uses a hovercraft system for maneuvering in broken mountain terrain, though tanks operate more efficiently in jungles and plains. Powered by an anti-matter system with about 25 years of energy life. Carries a small 3-foot (0.9 m) locker for personal effects plus a weapons locker with six energy rifles, six energy pistols, 24 E-Clips and 16 grenades.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.93-95'),
  ('evil-eye-apc', '"Evil Eye" APC (A-73)', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 3, 12, '200 mph (320 kmph) maximum, hovercraft system', 'Not possible; hover system will not lift the vehicle beyond 5 feet (1.5 m) off the surface', NULL, 'Height: 11 feet (3.3 m). Width: 9 feet (2.7 m). Length: 15 feet (4.5 m).', '15 tons fully loaded', 400, NULL, 'Not for sale; no price given for captured units.', 'A troop carrier/fighting vehicle whose boxy design recalls the 20th Century M-113, but floats on an air cushion instead of tracks and has a slightly curved front. It carries no turret; instead the front ''Eye'' is a short-range particle-beam irradiator that melts or disintegrates nearly everything in front of it to clear a landing zone for dismounting troops. Additional weapons are a pintle-mounted tri-beam machinegun (the gunner must expose himself through a hatch to use it) and two side-mounted mini-missile launchers. Firing slits on the sides let troops fire from both sides. Troop capacity: 12 soldiers in combat armor, or 8 in power armor. Powered by an anti-matter system with about 25 years of energy life. Cargo is the troop compartment (12 troops with equipment) or, substituted, 5 tons of cargo.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.95-96'),
  ('spikefish-attack-fighter', 'Spikefish Attack Fighter (AF-89)', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 1, 0, 'Not possible', 'Mach 2 in an atmosphere, Mach 8 in space; no altitude limit, can reach outer space; must cool off after 12 hours of flight in an atmosphere', NULL, 'Height: 6 feet (1.8 m); landing wheels extended add 2 feet (0.6 m). Width: 12 feet (3.65 m) tip to tip. Length: 8 feet (2.4 m).', '1 ton fully loaded', 300, NULL, 'Not for sale; no Spikefish has ever been captured in any shape to be resold.', 'The main attack fighter in the Arkhon arsenal, air- and space-capable, flown in attack wings alongside Stormwind and Ghost Wasp power armor troopers. Typical attack load is 2-4 long-range missiles and 4-8 medium-range missiles, plus four tri-beam guns. Powered by an anti-matter system with about 20 years of energy life. Cargo is essentially none; the pilot has room only for a sidearm. The reinforced pilot''s compartment doubles as an escape pod, airtight with 20 hours of life support, that can parachute to safety in atmosphere or float in space.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.96-97'),
  ('counterstrike-power-armor', 'Counterstrike Power Armor (APA-100)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running: 100 mph (160 kmph)', 'Flying: 600 mph (960 kmph) maximum; unlimited range, max altitude 40,000 feet (12,192 m)', NULL, 'Height: 10 feet (3.0 m); Width: 7 feet (2.1 m), 9 feet (2.4 m) with side wings/missile launchers; Length: 4 feet (1.2 m)', '1 ton', 550, NULL, 'Not for sale.', 'The primary power armor of the Megaversal Legion, a large humanoid exoskeleton on the line between power armor and robot, flown by a contra-gravity/inertia beam (I-Beam) propulsion system that the Dakir deliberately speed-limited. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 40. Powered by an anti-matter cell with about 30 years of average energy life; no cargo space. Carries an I-Beam gatling gun, a plasma blaster, wing-mounted mini-missiles, twin torso lasers, shoulder grenade launchers, and retractable double wrist energy blades, and can also fight hand to hand.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.116-117'),
  ('neo-abrams-m10a1-main-battle-tank', 'Neo-Abrams M10A1 Main Battle Tank', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Four; commander, pilot and two gunners', NULL, 'Driving on the ground: 300 mph (480 kmph) via hovercraft propulsion; inertia field allows 45-degree turns at any speed, 90-degree turns above 100 mph (160 kmph)', 'Flying: Not possible; hovercraft lifts the tank up to 7 feet (2.1 m) above a surface', 'Cannot travel over water deeper than 5 feet (1.5 m) or it will sink; can cross swamp and mud', 'Height: 14 feet (4.25 m); Width: 18 feet (5.4 m); Length: 36 feet (10.9 m)', '160 tons', 850, NULL, 'Not for sale; some nations would pay over 200 million credits for a new, undamaged tank. Stat block heads the model MBT-10A1, disagreeing with the section heading''s M10A1 -- book slip kept as printed.', 'The Megaversal Legion''s main tank, based on the pre-Rifts M1A3 Abrams but built around a hovercraft propulsion system in place of tracks, giving 300 mph ground speed. Fires I-Beam accelerated 120mm cannon rounds (sabot, high explosive, canister) from an auto-loading magazine, plus a coaxial grenade launcher, mini-missiles, a cupola plasma machinegun, a bow plasma machinegun, and side-mounted medium-range missiles. Protected by thick M.D.C. armor plus an energy force field. Powered by anti-matter with about 30 years average energy life; carries a small personal-effects locker and a weapons locker of four rifles, 16 E-Clips and 20 grenades.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.117-119'),
  ('neo-bradley-m6-ifv-scout-vehicle', 'Neo-Bradley M6-IFV Scout Vehicle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Two; a gunner and a pilot', 'Troop Capacity: 10 human-sized soldiers in body armor, or 6 Ojahee soldiers/power armor troopers; the M6S scout variant only carries 2 humans or 1 Ojahee/power armor trooper', 'Driving on the ground: 300 mph (480 kmph) via hovercraft propulsion', 'Flying: Not possible; hovercraft lifts up to 7 feet (2.1 m) above a surface', 'Can cross swamp, mud, rivers and lakes only at 100 mph (160 km) or greater, or it will sink; sinks if it travels more than a mile over water', 'Height: 12 feet (3.65 m); Width: 14 feet (4.25 m); Length: 30 feet (9.1 m)', '60 tons', 450, NULL, 'Not for sale; some nations would pay over 100 million credits for a new, undamaged vehicle.', 'A hovercraft infantry fighting vehicle and troop carrier built alongside the Neo-Abrams, printed as Model Type M6-IFV, with an M6S-IFV scout variant that trades troop capacity for slightly heavier armor. Armed with a light plasma cannon in the turret, a coaxial grenade launcher, and two side-mounted medium-range missile launchers. Protected by an energy force field. Powered by anti-matter with about 30 years average energy life; weapons locker holds 8 rifles, 40 E-Clips and 40 grenades.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.119-120'),
  ('neo-apache-ah-50-attack-aerodyne', 'Neo-Apache AH-50 Attack Aerodyne', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Four; pilot, co-pilot/gunner, sensor operator and secondary gunner', NULL, 'Driving on the ground: Not possible', 'Flying: Mach 3 (2010 mph/3234 kmph) maximum; speeds rarely exceed 100 mph (160 kmph) against ground targets; unlimited range limited only by pilot endurance; maximum altitude 30,000 feet (9144 m)', NULL, 'Height: 12 feet (3.65 m); Width: 8 feet (2.4 m); Length: 35 feet (11 m)', '8 tons', 400, NULL, 'Not for sale.', 'A contra-gravity gunship/fighter built to replace the pre-Rifts Apache helicopter without vulnerable rotors, able to reach Mach 3 and fight both ground and air targets. Carries a nose gatling plasma cannon, long-range, medium-range and mini-missile launchers, and two wing-mounted I-Beam machineguns, plus a light force field. Powered by anti-matter with about 30 years average energy life; small personal-effects compartment and a weapons locker of four energy rifles, 12 E-Clips and 20 grenades.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.120-121'),
  ('mecha-lizard-power-armor', 'Mecha-Lizard Power Armor (PA-10ML)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running: 80 mph (129 kmph) maximum, cruising 60 mph (96 kmph); does not fatigue the pilot; Leaping: 20 ft (6.1 m) standing, up to 40 ft (12.2 m) with a running start', 'Flying: Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 9 feet 7 inches (2.9 m); Width: 6 feet (1.8 m); Length: 20 feet (6.1 m) head to tail', 'One ton', 320, 10000000, '10 million credits.', 'A Santiago-built power armor shaped after the velociraptor-like Blood Lizard, with a slashing tail and sonic-scream weapon that mimics the beast''s cry. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 30. Carries a rifle-shaped multi-weapon combining a heavy laser and a grenade launcher/mortar, two mini-missile launchers, twin wrist ion blasters, and a jaw-mounted sonic pulse cannon that can stun or shatter armor. Nuclear powered with about 15 years average energy life; also has claw, bite and kick hand to hand attacks. Printed model number PA-10ML; the OCR text reads it as PA-1OML.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.168-171'),
  ('toro-minotaur-power-armor', 'Toro "Minotaur" Power Armor (TPA-7)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running: 70 mph (112 kmph); Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) standing, up to 30 ft (9.1 m) with a running start', 'Flying: Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 9 feet (2.7 m); Width: 6 feet (1.8 m); Length: 4 feet (1.2 m)', 'One ton (2,000 lb.)', 450, 8000000, '8 million credits.', 'A ten-year-old Cordoba assault power armor styled after a bull, with a head/helmet shaped like a bull''s and laser-firing horns. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 45. Carries shoulder mini-missiles, back-mounted medium-range missile tubes, forearm ion blasters, and normally an energy axe (swappable for rail guns, heavy lasers or similar weapons). Nuclear powered with about 15 years average energy life; thousands are in Cordoba military service.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.171-173'),
  ('glitter-boy-number-7', 'Glitter Boy Number 7 (AA-GB7)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running: 70 mph (112 kmph) maximum; running only tires the pilot at 20% of normal fatigue rate; Leaping: 10 ft (3.0 m) high or 15 ft (4.6 m) lengthwise from a short run', 'Flying: Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 9 feet (2.7 m), or 10 feet (3.0 m) with guns raised; Width: 4 feet (1.2 m); Length: 4 feet (1.2 m) including ammo drum', '1 ton fully loaded', 700, 30000000, '30 million credits for a new, undamaged GB-7 with all weapon systems; drops 10 million if one main weapon system is missing, or for rebuilt suits (which also permanently lose 10% M.D.C.). Good availability in Cordoba, Santiago and Arequipa; poor elsewhere.', 'A South American-built lighter, more form-fitting Glitter Boy variant that can be customized to each wearer, including female pilots as "Glitter Girls." Unlike the standard G-10, it carries two heavy shoulder weapons -- a variable-frequency laser cannon and a rail gun gatling -- plus two hip lasers, instead of a single Boom Gun; it cannot mount a Boom Gun since it lacks recoil dampening thrusters. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 30. Nuclear powered with about 20 years average energy life; the Santiago army fields over 500 of them.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.173-175'),
  ('mastodon-battle-robot', 'Mastodon Battle Robot (SHAB-10)', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Five; pilot, copilot/gunner, and three gunners (main gunner mans the Boom Gun turret)', '2 additional human-sized passengers could be squeezed in if absolutely necessary', 'Driving on the ground: 70 mph (112 kmph)', 'Flying: Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 35 feet (10.6 m); Width: 20 feet (6.1 m); Length: 40 feet (12.2 m)', '160 tons fully loaded', 950, 200000000, '200 million credits.', 'Officially named the "Hannibal," this is Cordoba''s mastodon/war-elephant-shaped super-heavy assault robot, second only to the Galapagos in size among South American war machines. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 55. Its trunk ends in an energized morning-star flail, its tusks are laser cannons, a head turret carries a vehicle-scale Boom Gun, and it mounts long-range missiles, a belly particle beam, and mini-missile MLRS boxes; its ears hide "Death Mirror" flash weapons that can trigger stunning or epileptic convulsions. Nuclear powered with about 10 years average energy life; nearly 200 are in Cordoba service.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.175-177'),
  ('galapagos-submersible-robot', 'Galapagos Submersible Robot (GATV-5)', 'rifts', 'robot', '14; commander, pilot, navigator/copilot, communications/sensors officer, 2 engineers and 8 gunners; can operate with a skeleton crew of 4-6, leaving most weapon systems to automatic fire control', 'Troop Capacity: 3 Hussar APCs and their 12 troops each, 8 Toro Power Armor, 4 Glitter Boys of either make, and 80 infantry soldiers; alternately the APCs can be swapped for 20 unmounted troopers, or up to 7 Hussars for 84 mechanized soldiers plus power-armored troopers', 'Driving on the ground: 50 mph (80.4 kmph)', 'Flying: 200 mph (320 kmph), or 300 mph (480 kmph) with head and legs fully retracted; sustainable safely for about an hour, with a 2-3 hour cooling-off period after, or a rising chance per 5 minutes over that of burning out the flight systems (1D4+2 weeks and 4D6 million credits to repair)', 'Underwater: 20 mph (32 kmph/17.2 knots) dived, or 25 mph (40 kmph) on the surface', 'Height: 70 feet (21.3 m); Width: 120 feet (36.5 m); Length: 250 feet (76.5 m)', '1500 tons fully loaded', 1800, 550000000, 'Not for sale to individuals; approximately 550 million credits for the governments of Cordoba and Santiago.', 'The largest and most powerful robot design in South America, a giant-turtle-shaped ultra-heavy combat robot able to travel on land, on and under water, and fly for limited periods. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 60. Its retractable head/turret carries twin heavy laser cannons, a quad rail gun, and medium-range missiles; three ion cannon turrets and four missile/laser batteries are set around the retractable shell. Nuclear powered with about 10 years average energy life; Cordoba fields 89 and Santiago 63, and a captured, permanently damaged unit (M.D.C. reduced 20%) serves as a Larhold war band''s flagship.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.177-179'),
  ('puma-class-medium-battle-tank', 'Puma-Class Medium Battle Tank (Cordoba/Santiago)', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Four', NULL, 'Driving on the ground: 100 mph (160 kmph) maximum on level terrain; 60 mph (96 kmph) maximum safe speed off-road, with a cumulative 10% chance per hour of jumping a tread above that', 'Flying: Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 9 feet (2.7 m), 10 feet (3.0 m) counting the rail gun cupola; Width: 8 feet (2.4 m); Length: 12 feet (3.65 m)', '30 tons fully loaded', 550, 1500000, '1.5 million credits with a combustion or electrical engine; 10 million credits with a nuclear engine. Sold only to reputable military organizations; captured/stolen tanks (typically 20% less M.D.C., missing the SLAS and one other weapon system) can be had for about half price.', 'A joint Cordoba/Santiago pre-Rifts-derived medium tank, range 500 miles (800 km) on combustion or electrical power (or nuclear). Its turret combines a 120mm cannon with an under-slung missile launcher, a pop-up Strobe Laser Array System (SLAS) that can engage up to ten targets or intercept missiles, a top rail gun cupola, and side rail gun and mini-missile mini-turrets. Weapons locker holds four rifles, 20 E-Clips and 20 grenades; carries 4 spare treads.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.180-181'),
  ('hussar-apc', 'Hussar APC (Cordoba and Santiago)', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Two; a driver and a gunner', 'Troop Capacity: 8 soldiers in body armor or 6 troopers in power armor', 'Driving on the ground: 100 mph (160 kmph) maximum on level terrain; 60 mph (96 kmph) maximum safe speed off-road, with a cumulative 10% chance per hour of jumping a tread above that', 'Flying: Not possible', NULL, 'Height: 8 feet (2.4 m); Width: 8 feet (2.4 m); Length: 10 feet (3.0 m)', '15 tons fully loaded', 280, 1000000, '1 million credits with a combustion or electrical engine; 10 million credits with a nuclear engine. Sold only to reputable military organizations; captured/stolen tanks (typically 20% less M.D.C., missing one other weapon system) can be had for half price.', 'A companion vehicle to the Puma tank, built from the same joint Cordoba/Santiago project, carrying 8 troops with light turret armament: a rail gun and a mini-missile launcher on each side. Range 550 miles (880 km) on combustion or electrical power (or nuclear). Weapons locker holds eight rifles, three missile launchers, 60 E-Clips and 40 grenades; carries 4 spare treads.', 'Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 p.182-183');

